---
import StaticPage from '../layouts/StaticPage.astro';

const lastUpdated = new Date().toLocaleDateString('en-IN', { day: '2-digit', month: 'long', year: 'numeric' });
---

<StaticPage
  title="Terms & Conditions — BooksPDF"
  description="The terms and conditions governing use of BooksPDF."
  eyebrow="Legal"
  heading="Terms & Conditions"
  subheading={`Last updated: ${lastUpdated} · Effective: January 1, 2025`}
>
  <div class="space-y-8 text-sm leading-relaxed text-[var(--ink-soft)]">
    <div class="rounded-ticket border border-stamp-red/30 bg-stamp-red/5 p-4 text-stamp-red">
      Important: if you do not agree to these terms, you must not access or use our services.
    </div>

    <section>
      <p>
        Welcome to BooksPDF. These Terms and Conditions ("Terms") govern your access to and use of our
        website, services, and products. By accessing or using BooksPDF, you agree to be bound by these
        Terms.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-semibold text-[var(--ink)]">1. Definitions</h2>
      <ul class="mt-2 list-disc space-y-1 pl-5">
        <li>"Service" refers to the BooksPDF website and all related services</li>
        <li>"User," "you," "your" refers to the individual accessing or using the Service</li>
        <li>"Content" refers to text, images, eBooks, and other materials available on the Service</li>
        <li>"Purchase" refers to the transaction of buying an eBook through our platform</li>
        <li>"Account" refers to your registered user account on BooksPDF</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-semibold text-[var(--ink)]">2. Acceptance of terms</h2>
      <p class="mt-2">By creating an account, making a purchase, or using our Service, you confirm that:</p>
      <ul class="mt-2 list-disc space-y-1 pl-5">
        <li>You are at least 18 years of age or have parental consent</li>
        <li>You have the legal capacity to enter into binding contracts</li>
        <li>You will comply with all applicable laws and regulations</li>
        <li>You have read and agree to our Privacy Policy</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-semibold text-[var(--ink)]">3. Account registration</h2>
      <p class="mt-2 font-medium text-[var(--ink)]">3.1 Account creation</p>
      <p class="mt-1">To access certain features, you must create an account. You agree to:</p>
      <ul class="mt-2 list-disc space-y-1 pl-5">
        <li>Provide accurate, current, and complete information</li>
        <li>Maintain and update your information to keep it accurate</li>
        <li>Maintain the security of your password</li>
        <li>Accept responsibility for all activities under your account</li>
        <li>Notify us immediately of any unauthorized use</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="mt-3 font-medium text-[var(--ink)]">3.2 Account suspension</p>
      <p class="mt-1">We reserve the right to suspend or terminate your account if you violate these Terms or engage in fraudulent activity.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-semibold text-[var(--ink)]">4. Use of service</h2>
      <p class="mt-2 font-medium text-[var(--ink)]">4.1 Permitted use</p>
      <ul class="mt-2 list-disc space-y-1 pl-5">
        <li>Browse and search for eBooks</li>
        <li>Purchase and download eBooks for personal use</li>
        <li>Access your purchased content through your account</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="mt-3 font-medium text-[var(--ink)]">4.2 Prohibited use</p>
      <ul class="mt-2 list-disc space-y-1 pl-5">
        <li>Redistribute, resell, or share downloaded eBooks</li>
        <li>Remove copyright notices or watermarks</li>
        <li>Use automated systems to scrape content</li>
        <li>Attempt to hack or compromise the Service</li>
        <li>Upload malware or viruses</li>
        <li>Engage in fraudulent activities</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-semibold text-[var(--ink)]">5. Purchases and payments</h2>
      <p class="mt-2 font-medium text-[var(--ink)]">5.1 Pricing</p>
      <ul class="mt-2 list-disc space-y-1 pl-5">
        <li>All prices are in Indian Rupees (INR)</li>
        <li>Prices are inclusive of applicable taxes</li>
        <li>We reserve the right to change prices at any time</li>
        <li>Price changes do not affect completed purchases</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="mt-3 font-medium text-[var(--ink)]">5.2 Payment processing</p>
      <ul class="mt-2 list-disc space-y-1 pl-5">
        <li>Payments are processed securely through PhonePe</li>
        <li>We do not store your payment card details</li>
        <li>Failed transactions may take 5–7 business days to refund</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="mt-3 font-medium text-[var(--ink)]">5.3 Delivery</p>
      <p class="mt-1">Digital products are delivered instantly upon successful payment, via the payment success page, your "My Library" section, and an email confirmation.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-semibold text-[var(--ink)]">6. Refund policy</h2>
      <div class="mt-2 rounded-ticket border border-marigold/30 bg-marigold/5 p-4 text-marigold-dark">
        Digital products: due to their nature, sales are generally final — but we offer refunds in specific circumstances.
      </div>
      <p class="mt-3 font-medium text-[var(--ink)]">6.1 Refund eligibility — you may request a refund if:</p>
      <ul class="mt-2 list-disc space-y-1 pl-5">
        <li>The file is corrupted or cannot be opened</li>
        <li>You were charged multiple times for the same purchase</li>
        <li>The book content significantly differs from its description</li>
        <li>You did not download the book within 48 hours of purchase</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="mt-3 font-medium text-[var(--ink)]">6.2 Refund process</p>
      <ul class="mt-2 list-disc space-y-1 pl-5">
        <li>Submit a refund request within 7 days of purchase</li>
        <li>Provide your transaction ID and reason for the refund</li>
        <li>Refunds are processed within 7–14 business days to your original payment method</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="mt-3">See our full <a href="/refund-policy" class="text-[var(--accent)] underline">Refund Policy</a> for details.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-semibold text-[var(--ink)]">7. Intellectual property rights</h2>
      <p class="mt-2 font-medium text-[var(--ink)]">7.1 Our content</p>
      <p class="mt-1">All content on BooksPDF, including text, graphics, logos, and software, is owned by us or our licensors and protected by copyright law.</p>
      <p class="mt-3 font-medium text-[var(--ink)]">7.2 eBook license</p>
      <p class="mt-1">When you purchase an eBook, you receive a limited, non-exclusive, non-transferable license to download and view it on your personal devices, and make backup copies for personal use. You may NOT reproduce, distribute, or publicly display the eBook, create derivative works, transfer or sell your license, or remove copyright notices.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-semibold text-[var(--ink)]">8. Limitation of liability</h2>
      <ul class="mt-2 list-disc space-y-1 pl-5">
        <li>BooksPDF is not liable for any indirect, incidental, or consequential damages</li>
        <li>Our total liability shall not exceed the amount you paid for the specific eBook</li>
        <li>We do not guarantee uninterrupted or error-free service</li>
        <li>We are not responsible for third-party content or links</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-semibold text-[var(--ink)]">9. Disclaimer of warranties</h2>
      <div class="mt-2 rounded-ticket border border-[var(--border)] bg-[var(--bg-soft)] p-4">
        <p class="font-semibold uppercase text-[var(--ink)]">The service is provided "as is" and "as available" without warranties of any kind.</p>
        <p class="mt-2">We disclaim all warranties, express or implied, including merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose, and non-infringement.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-semibold text-[var(--ink)]">10. Indemnification</h2>
      <p class="mt-2">You agree to indemnify and hold harmless BooksPDF, its affiliates, and their officers, directors, employees, and agents from claims arising from your use of the Service, violation of these Terms, violation of third-party rights, or fraudulent activity on your account.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-semibold text-[var(--ink)]">11. Governing law</h2>
      <p class="mt-2">These Terms are governed by the laws of India. Any disputes shall be subject to the exclusive jurisdiction of the courts in Mumbai, Maharashtra, India.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-semibold text-[var(--ink)]">12. Changes to terms</h2>
      <p class="mt-2">We may modify these Terms at any time. We'll update the "Last Updated" date, notify you via email or website notice, and material changes take effect 30 days after notification. Continued use of the Service means you accept the new Terms.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-semibold text-[var(--ink)]">13. Termination</h2>
      <p class="mt-2 font-medium text-[var(--ink)]">13.1 By you</p>
      <p class="mt-1">You may terminate your account any time via customer support. Your account deactivates within 48 hours, and you'll lose access to purchased content — download your purchases first, as no refund is given for unused balance.</p>
      <p class="mt-3 font-medium text-[var(--ink)]">13.2 By us</p>
      <p class="mt-1">We may suspend or terminate accounts that violate these Terms, engage in fraud, remain inactive for over 2 years, or as required by law.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-semibold text-[var(--ink)]">14. Dispute resolution</h2>
      <p class="mt-2">Before filing a claim, please contact us at <a href="mailto:contact@booksnpdf.com" class="text-[var(--accent)] underline">contact@booksnpdf.com</a> to resolve the issue informally. If informal resolution fails, disputes are resolved through binding arbitration under the Indian Arbitration and Conciliation Act, 1996. You agree to resolve disputes individually and waive participation in class actions.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-semibold text-[var(--ink)]">15–16. Severability & entire agreement</h2>
      <p class="mt-2">If any provision of these Terms is found invalid, the remaining provisions continue in full force. These Terms, together with our Privacy Policy and Refund Policy, constitute the entire agreement between you and BooksPDF.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-semibold text-[var(--ink)]">17. Contact information</h2>
      <div class="mt-2 rounded-ticket border border-[var(--border)] bg-[var(--bg-soft)] p-5">
        <p class="font-semibold text-[var(--ink)]">BooksPDF Legal Team</p>
        <p class="mt-2">Email: <a href="mailto:contact@booksnpdf.com" class="text-[var(--accent)] underline">contact@booksnpdf.com</a></p>
        <p>Address: 123 Book Street, Andheri East, Mumbai, Maharashtra 400069, India</p>
        <p class="mt-2 text-xs">Business hours: Monday – Saturday, 9:00 AM – 6:00 PM IST</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <div class="rounded-ticket bg-[var(--ink)] p-6 text-[var(--bg)]">
      <p class="font-semibold">By using BooksPDF, you acknowledge that you have read, understood, and agree to be bound by these Terms and Conditions.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</StaticPage>
